.TH WEZTERM-MOVE-TAB 1 "2026-07-04" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wezterm-move-tab \- request a WezTerm or parent tmux tab move
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wezterm-move-tab
.RI [ left | right ]
.RI [ tty ]
.br
.B wezterm-move-tab
.RI [ left | right ]
.B --tty
.I tty
.br
.B wezterm-move-tab
.B --parent
.RI [ left | right ]
.RI [ tty ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wezterm-move-tab
emits a WezTerm OSC 1337
.B SetUserVar
request for moving the current tab. Consumers such as tmux can bind keys to
this helper when the focused application cannot handle the key itself.
.PP
Normal requests set
.B DOT_MOVE_TAB
and are handled by the outer WezTerm process. Parent requests set
.B DOT_PARENT_MOVE_TAB
inside tmux DCS passthrough framing so the request can escape an inner tmux and
be translated by WezTerm into the parent tmux layer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --tty \fItty\fR
Write the request to
.I tty
instead of
.B $WEZTERM_MOVE_TAB_TTY
or
.B /dev/tty .
.TP
.B --parent
Bubble the move request to the parent tmux layer.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B left
Move the current tab or tmux window left.
.TP
.B right
Move the current tab or tmux window right. This is the default.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
wezterm-move-tab left /dev/ttys001
wezterm-move-tab right --tty /dev/ttys001
wezterm-move-tab --parent left /dev/ttys001
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The request was written.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wezterm-switch-tab (1)
